  "raw_text": "238\n\nTaitil\n \n(\ndb,dictu-alt\n;\n \nTaitel\n-\ndict,dictu\n;\n \nTaikil\n-\njw\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ntitle, last name, family name\n \n/ título, apellido\n\nAisanka taitilka\n \n(a/t:\n \nAisanka lalka\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntheme (of a talk or discourse)\n \n/ tema (de un discurso)\n\nTaitus\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nTaitusra\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nTitus\n \n(Bible book) / Tito (libro bíblico)\n\nTak\n \n–\n \nall, all that is left, all that is remaining\n \n/ todo, todo lo que queda\n\nTâka\n \n(1)\n \n–\n \nconstruct of/de:\n \nTâ\n \n–\n \nbeginning, extremity, tip, point\n \n/ principio, extremidad, punta, punto\n\nUlbanka tâka\n \n(Ulbanka taka)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nappendix\n \n/ apéndice\n\nTaka\n \n(2) (a/t:\n \nTâka\n-db\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nremainder of, what is left of, what remains of, balance of, remnant of, residue of, rest of,\ncontinuation of, portion of, part of\n \n/ resto de, lo que queda de, balance de, remanente de, residuo de, resto de,\ncontinuación de, porción de, parte de\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh19\n):\n \nBaibil taka kum\n \n–\n \na portion of the Bible\n \n/ una porción de la biblia\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n49:6\n)\n:\n \nIsrael\n \nt\nâ\nka kau b\nâ\nra ba\n \n–\n \nthose still remaining of Israel\n \n/ los que aún quedan de Israel\n)\n\nTaka\n \n(3) (n-connective construct of Takaia / s-construct conexivo de Takaia)\n \n–\n \noccurrence, happening, event, something\nthat happened\n \n/ suceso, hecho,\n \nacontecimiento\n, algo que paso\n\n(Ex/Ej\n):\n \n¿Dîa taka mita King Ezequías ba sari pali inan?\n \n–\n \nBecause of what ha\np\npening did King Hezekiah weep?\n \n/\n \n¿Por qué suceso\n\nlloró\n \nel rey Ezequías\n \ndesconsoladamente\n?\n)\n\nTakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become, to appear, to happen, to come to be, to come to do, to occur, to issue from, to depart, to go out\n \n/\nvolverse, aparecer, pasar, suceder, venir a ser, venir a hacer, ocurrir, salir\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nDîa muni diara saura wan takisa?\n \n–\n \nWhy do bad things happen to us?\n \n/ ¿Por qué nos pasan cosas malas?)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nDîa takisa?\n \n(short form / forma corta:\n \nDîa taksa?\n)\n \n–\n \nWhat’s happening?\n \n/ ¿Qué esta pasando?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nsgd5\n):\n \nTetragramáton ba, YHWH: “Witin Daukisa Diara nani Takbia”\n \n–\n \nThe Tetragrammaton, YHWH: “He Causes to Become”\n\n/ El Tetragrámaton, YHWH: ”Él hace que llegue a ser”\n)\n\nAihka takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto separate from, to become different, to be separated, to be different\n \n/ separarse, volverse\ndiferente, estar separado, ser diferente\n\nAihtabi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get baptized, to take a shower, to take a bath\n \n/ bautizarse, ducharse, bañarse\n \n(See also /\nVer también:\n \nTahbi daukaia\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: It is more common to use\n \nAihtabaia\n \ninstead of\n \nAihtabi takaia\n \nto say:\n \nto take a bath, to take a shower\n \n/ Es más\ncomún usar\n \nAihtabaia\n \nen lugar de\n \nAihtabi takaia\n \npara decir: ducharse, bañarse)\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nAihtabi takaia\n \ncan\n \nalso\n \nrefer to a spiritistic practice with a bucket shower. /\n \nAihtabi takaia\n \ntambién\n \npuede\n\nreferirse a una práctica espiritista con un ba\nñ\no con balde.)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n01/21\n):\n \nAihtabi takai nani ba “\nâ\nu” wibia taim, Jisas atki wan sakan mana ba kasak luki ba marikisa,\n \nbara ai\n\nkupia aiska ni ai rayaka Jehova ra yaban upla sut mawanra.\n \n–\n \nWhen those to be baptized say “yes”, they show in front of\n\nall people that they are exercising faith in Jesus’ ransom sacrifice and gave their life to Jehovah with their whole heart.\n \n/\n\nCuando los que se van a bautizar dicen \"sí\", muestran ante todas las personas que están ejerciendo fe en el sacrificio de\n\nrescate de Jesús y dieron su vida a Jehová con todo su corazón.)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n01/21\n):\n \nManis ra d\nî\na mita tukban sa aihtabi takaia\n \ndukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat has impelled many to become baptized?\n \n/\n\n¿Qué ha impulsado a muchos a bautizarse?)\n\nAihtabi takaia aisaia ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbaptism talk\n \n/ discurso de bautismo\n\nAihtabi takan kristian waitna, Aihtabi takan kristian mairin\n \n–\n \nbaptized brother, baptized sister\n \n/\nhermano bautizado, hermana bautizada\n\nAihtabi takras\n \n–\n \nnot baptized\n \n/ no bautizado\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nTahbi daukras\n)\n\nSmalki tataukra kau aihtabi takras\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nunbaptized publisher\n \n/ publicador no bautizado\n\nAilal takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become many, to become abundant\n \n/ hacerse muchos, hacerse abundantes\n\nAisubi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be born\n \n/ nacer\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nAni ra aisubi takram?\n \n–\n \nWhere were you born?\n \n/ ¿Dónde naciste?)\n\nAisubi takan\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado\n)\n \n–\n \nborn\n \n/\n \nnació, nacido\n\nAlmuk takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become old\n \n/ envejecer\n\nAlmuk takan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \naging\n \n/ envejecimiento\n\nAntin takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hunt\n \n/ cazar\n\nAntin tatakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nhunter\n \n/ cazador\n\nAsla takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto organize together, to come to be together\n \n/ organizarse juntos, venir a estar juntos\n\n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAsla aidrubaia\n \n–\n \nto meet together\n \n/ reunirse)\n\nAsla takanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \norganization, institution\n \n/ organización, institución\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n):\n \nAsla takanka p\nâ\nwanka nani\n \n–\n \nOrganizational Accomplishments\n \n/ Logros de la organización)",
